# Ticket pipeline (pointer)

Active **GitHub issue `#N`** and/or **open PR** work follows a **fixed stage order**. Track a **pointer** to the current stage. Advance forward only when that stage passes. **Any code fix rewinds the pointer to `BUGBOT`** (then move forward again).

Adapted from Integral / SmartAstro workflow for this marketing-site repo.

## Stages (in order)

```
IMPLEMENT → BUGBOT → TESTS → ARCHITECT → DEPLOY
```

| Stage | What happens | Advance when |
|-------|----------------|--------------|
| **IMPLEMENT** | Ship code/docs for AC, review feedback, or CI fixes | Chunk ready for review → **BUGBOT** |
| **BUGBOT** | `/review-bugbot` · `Diff: branch changes` | **Clean** on current diff → **TESTS** |
| **TESTS** | `tests/*.test.js` (prefer issue refs in names); `npm test` / `node --test` for touched areas | **Pass** → **ARCHITECT** |
| **ARCHITECT** | Pre-merge gate: sync contract, HTML/JS layering, no scope creep | **Merge-ready** → **DEPLOY** |
| **DEPLOY** | Validate, push, PR with `Closes #N` when applicable; watch checks; merge **only when human asks** | Human **merge/sign-off** + issue closed → **exit** |

## Rewind rules (mandatory)

| Situation | Pointer moves to |
|-----------|------------------|
| Bugbot reports findings | Stay **BUGBOT** — fix, re-run Bugbot until clean |
| Tests fail or test fixes change behavior | **BUGBOT** |
| Architect reports blockers | **BUGBOT** — fix, re-run Bugbot → Tests → Architect |
| PR/CI/human review needs code changes | **IMPLEMENT** — then **BUGBOT** before skipping ahead |

**Never skip BUGBOT** after a code change, including session resume or post-architect fixes.

## Bug-class that must get a regression test

Schedule/popup/availability behavior (especially date windows, `hasEnded`, `removedScheduleIds`, dropdown rendering) **must** include a failing-then-passing unit test. These regressions look “fine today” and break tomorrow.

## Response format (active ticket)

End substantive work with:

**Pipeline:** `IMPLEMENT` | `BUGBOT` | `TESTS` | `ARCHITECT` | `DEPLOY` — plus Bugbot / tests / architect / deploy state and **next stage**.
